Building the package
====================

The packaging is on the branch "pisiworks", beside the code:

    gbp buildpackage

debian/gbp.conf makes the upstream tarball from that branch.

Rust
----
The programs need Rust 1.91 or newer (Cargo.toml: rust-version), because of
the interface library they are built on, GPUI. Debian 13 and Pardus 25 have
Rust 1.85, with which they do not build.

Building with no network
------------------------
The programs are built from some 700 Rust libraries (crates), which cargo
otherwise fetches from crates.io. debian/rules builds from the folder
cargo-vendor/ in the source tree when it is there, and then needs no network.

    packaging/vendor-tarball.sh

makes that folder and packs it as
target/deb/pisiworks_VERSION.orig-cargo-vendor.tar.xz (about 90 MB), the form
of an additional upstream tarball of a "3.0 (quilt)" source package. To build:

    cp pisiworks_VERSION.orig-cargo-vendor.tar.xz ..
    tar -xf ../pisiworks_VERSION.orig-cargo-vendor.tar.xz
    gbp buildpackage

cargo-vendor/ is not kept in git (.gitignore). gbp cannot make this tarball
itself (--git-component wants the folder in git), so it is unpacked by hand.

The files of the package are laid out by packaging/install-files.sh, which
packaging/build-deb.sh uses too: the two ways give the same package.

 -- Murat SAPMAZ
